Here's a minimal Express server in TypeScript:

```typescript
import express from 'express';

const app = express();
const PORT = 3000;

app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ message: 'Hello, World!' });
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

To run it:
```bash
npm install express
npx tsx server.ts
```

The server will respond with `{"message": "Hello, World!"}` at the root endpoint.

Great choice! Here's how to set up **PostgreSQL** for your project:

```bash
npm install pg @types/pg
```

```typescript
import { Pool } from 'pg';

const pool = new Pool({
  host: 'localhost',
  port: 5432,
  database: 'myapp',
  user: 'postgres',
  password: 'password',
});

export async function query(text: string, params?: any[]) {
  const result = await pool.query(text, params);
  return result.rows;
}
```

Your PostgreSQL connection is ready to use!
